XID[3-4-high-approach]XTYPE[joseki]XNAME[3-4 point · high approach]XALIAS[One-space high approach][Ikken takagakari][一間高ガカリ][Attach-drawback][Tsuke-hiki]XFAM[3-4 point/High approach]XDIFF[20k]XERA[classic][modern][ai]XSTART[setup]XTAG[approach][basic joseki]XSUM[White approaches the 3-4 stone high, on the 5-4 point. The usual answer is the inside attachment, hane and draw back (tsuke-hiki), one of the first joseki beginners learn. White then protects with a solid or a hanging connection. Sources: 34PointHighApproach, 34PointHighApproachInsideContact, 34PointHighApproachAttachDrawbackJoseki, 34PointHighApproachInsideContactHangingConnection.]XSRC[Sensei's Library (senseis.xmp.net), joseki pages listed in XSUM. Sequences copied from its diagrams and mirrored to the top-right corner.]PL[B]XST[start]XEV[=]XPW[{{TR:P16|White's high approach}} to {{TR:R16|the 3-4 stone}}. High approach on the 5-4 point: faces the center more than the low approach and leaves the corner to Black.]AB[qd]AW[od]
